      <h3>The Big Picture: 3–6 Months Overall</h3>
      <p>The complete process from initial application to receiving your Tarjeta de Identidad de Extranjero (TIE) and registering on the padrón typically takes between three and six months. This timeline includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Document preparation:</strong> 2–4 weeks (gathering requirements, translations, apostilles)</li>
        <li><strong>Consulate processing:</strong> 6–12 weeks (visa decision)</li>
        <li><strong>Entry to Spain:</strong> Within 90 days of visa approval</li>
        <li><strong>TIE application & processing:</strong> 1–3 weeks after arrival</li>
        <li><strong>Padrón registration:</strong> Same day to 1 week after application</li>
      </ul>

      <p>However, this timeline is not fixed. Delays can occur at any stage, and some applicants move faster. The most critical variable is how quickly you prepare and submit a complete application. Incomplete or incorrect applications can add weeks or even months to your timeline.</p>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--info">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">ℹ️</span>
        <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> To keep your timeline on track, submit a complete application with all required documents correctly translated and apostilled. Consulates cannot process applications missing even one document, which can delay your approval by 4–8 weeks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

